## Core Products

- [Prodigy Math](https://www.prodigygame.com/main-en/prodigy-math): Adaptive math practice set in a fantasy RPG world. Students answer curriculum-aligned questions to battle enemies, complete quests, and earn rewards. Covers hundreds of skills across grades 1–8. Teachers can assign content, run assessments, and track progress.
- [Prodigy English](https://www.prodigygame.com/main-en/prodigy-english): A world-building English game that develops reading and language skills. Students learn, gather resources, and construct their own world through structured literacy practice.
- [Math Facts Practice](https://www.prodigygame.com/main-en/math-facts-practice): Focused fluency practice for foundational math facts, integrated into the Prodigy experience.

## Audiences

- [For Teachers](https://www.prodigygame.com/main-en/teachers): Free, standards-aligned math and English games for grades 1–8. Teachers get one-click login, class rostering, assignments, reports, and motivational tools. Trusted by nearly 800,000 educators in 70,000+ schools. No cost to teachers or schools.
- [For Parents](https://www.prodigygame.com/main-en/parents): Tools to support children's math and English learning at home. The parent dashboard provides progress tracking, goal-setting, and insight into what skills kids are practising. Free to use; premium membership available.
- [For Administrators](https://www.prodigygame.com/main-en/administrators): District-wide adoption at no cost, including teacher professional development. Privacy-first and independently evaluated as one of the best platforms for student data safety and security.
- [For Homeschoolers](https://www.prodigygame.com/main-en/homeschoolers): Adaptive, standards-aligned math program designed for home learning. Offers flexibility of self-paced learning with real-time progress reports so parents don't need to be math experts. Prodigy is an approved vendor with ESA, Scholarship, and Grant programs — homeschooling families can use state funds to fully fund a Prodigy Ultra membership.

## Why Prodigy

- Game-based learning that students genuinely want to play, reducing resistance to practice
- Adaptive algorithm personalizes question difficulty and content to each student's level
- Curriculum-aligned to state and national standards across all 50 US states, Canada, and Australia
- Free core experience for all teachers, students, and schools — no budget required
- Proven results: students with heavy Prodigy use significantly outperformed peers in California end-of-year assessments

